<p>Near the image center, rotation about \(y\) and translation along \(x\) look nearly identical: for small \(x\) and \(y\), \(\dot{x} \approx -\omega_y\) and \(\dot{y} \approx 0\). The same holds for rotation about \(x\) and translation along \(y\), so the two are difficult to separate with a narrow field of view.</p>

